.key ARGS/F
;
; Launcher for pydiags — sets PYTHONHOME/PATH then runs it.
;
; AmigaDOS script arg syntax: .key ARGS/F takes the whole remainder of
; the command line as a single string named ARGS, then <ARGS> below
; expands to it. This matches how the OS4 shell parses `execute foo a b`.
;
; Headless (one-shot subcommand, printed then exit) works via execute:
;
;   execute DH1:scripts/pydiags hash
;   execute DH1:scripts/pydiags dns example.com
;   execute DH1:scripts/pydiags http http://example.com/
;
; INTERACTIVE MODE (menu TUI) — do NOT launch through `execute`.
; AmigaDOS execute closes stdin as soon as it is done reading the
; script itself, so pydiags input() returns EOF immediately and the
; TUI drops back to shell.  Launch directly instead:
;
;   ; setenv PYTHONHOME python3:
;   ; setenv PYTHONPATH python3:lib
;   python3 python3:examples/pydiags.py
;
; setenv PYTHONHOME python3:
; setenv PYTHONPATH python3:lib
python3 python3:examples/pydiags.py <ARGS>
